Phhbbt.                                                   (snappy comeback, eh?)

}>A fact that keeps getting totally ignored is that no student, faculty or staff
}>member is denied access to any newsgroup.  Get a username on the HDS.  I agree
}>the newsreader there is less fully-featured than the newsreaders on PV and
}>other systems.
}[...]

}I believe an account on WYLBER (the inconvenient HDS system) is only
}one requirement. User's must also sign a form saying that they want
}access to alt.sex, etc. (I.e. They must sign a "pervert list".)

Problems with using `Wylbur':

   * You must sign the `perverts list' -- the machine readable copy
     of which has been *proven* insecure.
   * You must pay to use Wylbur after a certain amount of use.
   * Wylbur newsreader extremely primitive.
   * Lack of short courses on the use of Wylbur.
   * Wylbur file system can't handle some files (long lines).
   * Wylbur lacks basic utilities (uudecode, shar, tar, uncompress).

Of course, it is no secret that I think this policy is extremely brain damaged.

